    "owner_kind": "org",
    "name": "sweep-git-repos",
    "version": "0.6.2",
    "description": "You have a folder of repos and no idea which hold work that exists only on your laptop. On the machine this was built on, one sweep found 83 repositories and 35 branches living only there. It walks every repo under one folder, reads unpushed commits, uncommitted changes, stashes and upstream-less branches, names any repository whose history carries a secret-shaped file, asks GitHub whether that work is on origin, compares with the last sweep and writes a digest. An unreadable repo is listed as unknown, not dropped. Without a GitHub token that leg is skipped with the fix named, and the sweep completes. Your repositories are only ever read from; it writes a baseline, drift record and digest outside them.",
    "author": "jayanth <jayanth.sms.in@gmail.com>",
    "visibility": "public"
  },
